Z||000003||william_thorniii||10-20-2000||11:27 AM||||This information is not new... but apparently some missed the several posts in the last week about them.  I received my pair of spindles on Wednesday from Street Dreams.  Don't get too excited.  As of my last conversation, they were only going to be able to have 7 sets done in the next few weeks.  They have been trying to get them done for almost a year now.  The problem is with the foundry... yada, yada, yada.  I was very happy to have received the FIRST customer pair since I have bothered them so much.  I intend to install them over the weekend.  Don't get too excited though... the pics won't turn out well, as the car is in the middle of a complete suspension massaging... and will be off of the ground for quite some time.  Perhaps I will be able to drop the front end for you guys.  Also another thing to note is that they cost $349 +SH not the $249 as was posted on their site last year.  This was due to a higher than anticipated development cost.  Either way it was a bargain for someone that needs good handling.  <P>Sorry for the long post...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
